{
  "id": "tlb-hit-miss",
  "title": "TLB Hits and Misses: The Cost of a Page Table Lookup",
  "eyebrow": "paging",
  "language": "en",
  "duration": 53,
  "topic": "Translation Lookaside Buffer — a tiny on-chip cache of recent virtual-to-physical translations; a hit returns the frame number in a single cycle, a miss walks the page table and then fills the cache, dramatically slower",
  "subject_id": "operativsystemer",
  "chapter_number": 5,
  "prerequisites": [
    "address-translation"
  ],
  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "manimoIntro",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 8.93,
      "narration": "Every memory access has to be translated. Doing that walk on every load would be ruinously slow — so the hardware keeps a tiny cheat sheet.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "center",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "manimo-enter",
            "content": "Manimo bobs in centre-screen",
            "delay": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "How do we make a page-table lookup cheap?",
            "delay": 0.7,
            "color": "var(--chalk-100)",
            "position": "below Manimo, serif italic"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "tlbCard",
      "start": 8.93,
      "end": 18.76,
      "narration": "The translation lookaside buffer is a small on-chip cache. Each entry maps a virtual page number to a physical frame number, with a valid bit on the side.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "center",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "TLB · translation lookaside buffer",
            "delay": 0,
            "color": "var(--amber-300)",
            "position": "small mono eyebrow"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "Four-row table with columns: VPN, PFN, valid",
            "delay": 0.4,
            "color": "var(--chalk-200)"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-label",
            "content": "Three rows pre-populated with VPN→PFN entries; one row empty",
            "delay": 1.2,
            "color": "var(--amber-400)"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hit",
      "start": 18.76,
      "end": 29.95,
      "narration": "A load asks for virtual page seven. The TLB has it, and answers in one cycle: frame ninety-two. Fast path — about ten nanoseconds.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "top-bottom",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "TLB HIT",
            "delay": 0,
            "color": "var(--teal-400)",
            "position": "small mono eyebrow"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "Virtual address tile glides toward the TLB; matching row lights up",
            "delay": 0.6,
            "color": "var(--teal-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-label",
            "content": "Frame number leaves the TLB to a 'physical address' box on the right",
            "delay": 2.6,
            "color": "var(--teal-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "≈ 10 ns · one memory cycle",
            "delay": 4,
            "color": "var(--chalk-100)",
            "position": "below path, mono"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "miss",
      "start": 29.95,
      "end": 42.74,
      "narration": "A load asks for virtual page nineteen. Not in the TLB. The hardware walks the page table in memory, finds frame thirty-four, fills a TLB slot, and only then completes the access.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "top-bottom",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "TLB MISS",
            "delay": 0,
            "color": "var(--rose-400)",
            "position": "small mono eyebrow"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "Address tile arrives at TLB, no row lights up",
            "delay": 0.6,
            "color": "var(--rose-300)"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "Dotted path branches down to a page-table box; lookup returns PFN",
            "delay": 2,
            "color": "var(--chalk-200)"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "PFN travels up, fills empty TLB row, then continues to physical-address box",
            "delay": 4.5,
            "color": "var(--amber-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "≈ 100 ns · table walk + fill",
            "delay": 6.5,
            "color": "var(--chalk-100)",
            "position": "below path, mono"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "takeaway",
      "start": 42.74,
      "end": 53,
      "narration": "Programs reuse a small set of pages, so most lookups hit the TLB — and a few cheap misses end up paying for themselves many times over.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "center",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "hit ≈ 10 ns · miss ≈ 100 ns",
            "delay": 0.3,
            "color": "var(--chalk-100)",
            "position": "centre, mono row"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "locality of reference is why this works",
            "delay": 1.4,
            "color": "var(--chalk-200)",
            "position": "serif italic caption"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "(hit rates of 95–99% are typical)",
